183
00:11:40,269 --> 00:11:42,310
<font color="#FFFFFF">You're loud.</font>

184
00:11:42,351 --> 00:11:47,269
<font color="#FFFFFF">All right, Steve, this is
exactly how your hotel room
looked in 1981.</font>

185
00:11:47,310 --> 00:11:49,393
<font color="#FFFFFF">Whoa! A water bed.</font>

186
00:11:51,768 --> 00:11:56,685
<font color="#FFFFFF">So, basically I just
concentrate as hard as I can
that I'm in 1981,</font>

187
00:11:56,727 --> 00:12:00,768
<font color="#FFFFFF">and I'll be transported
back in time to meet
my dream girl from the painting?</font>

188
00:12:00,810 --> 00:12:03,560
<font color="#FFFFFF">Yes, Steve.
What is so hard
to understand about that?</font>

189
00:12:04,685 --> 00:12:08,227
<font color="#FFFFFF">Okay. It's May 14, 1981.</font>

190
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:11,393
<font color="#FFFFFF">President Jimmy Carter leaves
the White House in disgrace.</font>

191
00:12:11,435 --> 00:12:15,518
<font color="#FFFFFF">Pope John Paul II
is shot in Rome
by a deranged Jimmy Carter.</font>

192
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:19,476
<font color="#FFFFFF">Jimmy Carter
kidnaps and devours
13 Christian babies.</font>

193
00:12:19,518 --> 00:12:23,144
<font color="#FFFFFF">Hmm. Maybe I should have
read a real history book
instead of the one Dad wrote.</font>

194
00:12:27,393 --> 00:12:29,727
<font color="#FFFFFF">Did it work?
Is it 1981?</font>

195
00:12:34,476 --> 00:12:37,269
<font color="#FFFFFF">Roger?
Damn it, it didn't work.</font>

196
00:12:37,310 --> 00:12:41,393
<font color="#FFFFFF">Who's Roger?
The name's Reaganomics
Lamborghini, Jacuzzi dealer.</font>

197
00:12:41,435 --> 00:12:44,768
<font color="#FFFFFF">Wanna smoke cocaine
out of my pipe
made from a Rubik's Cube?</font>

198
00:12:49,351 --> 00:12:51,144
<font color="#FFFFFF">Sir, are you all right?</font>

199
00:12:51,185 --> 00:12:53,518
<font color="#FFFFFF">I was sitting
on this water bed,
minding my own business,</font>

200
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:55,518
<font color="#FFFFFF">when it
spontaneously exploded.</font>

201
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:58,518
<font color="#FFFFFF">I demand a week of free rooms,
or I'll sue the crap out of you!</font>

202
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:00,227
<font color="#FFFFFF">Wait a second.</font>

203
00:13:04,310 --> 00:13:07,351
<font color="#FFFFFF">I made it!
It's 1981!</font>

204
00:13:16,935 --> 00:13:19,810
<font color="#FFFFFF">Hey, I just got
another crazy text
from Stan about socks.</font>

205
00:13:19,852 --> 00:13:22,518
<font color="#FFFFFF">Is he okay?
Oh, I'm sure he's fine.</font>

206
00:13:31,102 --> 00:13:33,935
<font color="#FFFFFF">Look, I don't have time
for anyone else right now.</font>

207
00:13:33,977 --> 00:13:36,269
<font color="#FFFFFF">I'm too busy
living my own life.</font>

208
00:13:36,310 --> 00:13:38,227
<font color="#FFFFFF">But it's not your life.
It belongs to…</font>

209
00:13:38,269 --> 00:13:40,185
<font color="#FFFFFF">Sarah!
Where have you been?</font>

210
00:13:40,227 --> 00:13:42,060
<font color="#FFFFFF">- You have
to give your speech.
- What?</font>

211
00:13:42,102 --> 00:13:44,518
<font color="#FFFFFF">There she is…</font>

212
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:49,144
<font color="#FFFFFF">our closing speaker,
OmniSlab rep, Sarah Blanch!</font>

213
00:13:49,185 --> 00:13:52,476
<font color="#FFFFFF">All right, you've taken Sarah
as far as she can go.
Let's make a run for it.</font>

214
00:13:52,518 --> 00:13:53,727
<font color="#FFFFFF">Come on up, Sarah.</font>

215
00:14:00,893 --> 00:14:03,727
<font color="#FFFFFF">You… dumb bitch.</font>

216
00:14:12,185 --> 00:14:13,560
<font color="#FFFFFF">Hello.</font>

217
00:14:13,601 --> 00:14:18,601
<font color="#FFFFFF">Um, I'm here to talk
about… rebar placement…</font>

218
00:14:18,643 --> 00:14:21,893
<font color="#FFFFFF">and planned gap
structure coordination.</font>

219
00:14:21,935 --> 00:14:23,310
<font color="#FFFFFF">Huh?</font>

220
00:14:26,601 --> 00:14:29,893
<font color="#FFFFFF">You know what? No.</font>

221
00:14:29,935 --> 00:14:35,060
<font color="#FFFFFF">What I'd really like
to talk about is
the, um… uh… uh… uh…</font>

222
00:14:37,185 --> 00:14:39,685
<font color="#FFFFFF">the Chinese.</font>

223
00:14:39,727 --> 00:14:44,518
<font color="#FFFFFF">The Chinese threat
to our domestic
concrete industry.</font>

224
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:48,851
<font color="#FFFFFF">There are over
a million Chinese people
in China alone.</font>

225
00:14:48,852 --> 00:14:52,560
<font color="#FFFFFF">And I'm here to tell you,
they are a-comin', folks.</font>

226
00:14:52,601 --> 00:14:55,393
<font color="#FFFFFF">They know math.
They know kung fu.</font>

227
00:14:55,435 --> 00:14:58,893
<font color="#FFFFFF">And they've been
going pee-pee
in our Coke for years!</font>

228
00:14:58,935 --> 00:15:02,518
<font color="#FFFFFF">So let's keep the yellow
out of our red,
white and blue!</font>

229
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:05,144
<font color="#FFFFFF">- Whoo-hoo!
- Way to go, Sarah!</font>

230
00:15:14,977 --> 00:15:17,144
<font color="#FFFFFF">Nagel, you're a genius.</font>

231
00:15:17,185 --> 00:15:19,185
<font color="#FFFFFF">Sun-faded prints
of your paintings…</font>

232
00:15:19,227 --> 00:15:22,019
<font color="#FFFFFF">will never be found
in Korean hair salons.</font>

233
00:15:25,269 --> 00:15:29,685
<font color="#FFFFFF">Mr. Nagel, sir,
I have traveled
a great distance to see you.</font>

234
00:15:29,727 --> 00:15:33,144
<font color="#FFFFFF">You paint
my dream girl today,
and I need to know who she is.</font>

235
00:15:33,185 --> 00:15:36,685
<font color="#FFFFFF">Oh, I'm touched
by your passion, young man.</font>

236
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:39,351
<font color="#FFFFFF">I'll help you
on your lover's quest.</font>

237
00:15:39,393 --> 00:15:43,019
<font color="#FFFFFF">But first,
share in some cherry wine.</font>

238
00:15:45,685 --> 00:15:48,852
<font color="#FFFFFF">Um, cherry wine
tastes pretty weird.</font>

239
00:15:48,893 --> 00:15:53,310
<font color="#FFFFFF">That's because I put
a bunch of weird,
illegal things in it.</font>

240
00:15:55,977 --> 00:15:58,643
<font color="#FFFFFF">Nagel, you son of a bitch,
let's drug some kids.</font>

241
00:16:00,102 --> 00:16:03,019
<font color="#FFFFFF">Oh, you kidding me?
You already cut the turkey?</font>

242
00:16:05,768 --> 00:16:09,435
<font color="#FFFFFF">Well, Sarah, it's been fun,
but all good characters
must come to an end.</font>

243
00:16:09,476 --> 00:16:12,893
<font color="#FFFFFF">Sarah. Jed Farnsworth
of the Cherino
Concrete Corporation.</font>

244
00:16:12,935 --> 00:16:14,977
<font color="#FFFFFF">I haven't heard
someone speak
with that much passion…</font>

245
00:16:15,019 --> 00:16:17,310
<font color="#FFFFFF">since my fat friend
discovered Buca di Beppo.</font>

246
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:19,643
<font color="#FFFFFF">Wow. Thank you.</font>

247
00:16:19,685 --> 00:16:22,727
<font color="#FFFFFF">Look, I want you
to come manage
my Portland facility.</font>

248
00:16:22,768 --> 00:16:25,810
<font color="#FFFFFF">It's the most
prestigious job
in the concrete industry.</font>

249
00:16:25,852 --> 00:16:28,560
<font color="#FFFFFF">I… I don't know
what to say.</font>

250
00:16:28,601 --> 00:16:32,060
<font color="#FFFFFF">Say yes, and tomorrow
you can fly to your new life
in Economy Plus,</font>

251
00:16:32,102 --> 00:16:35,601
<font color="#FFFFFF">with only one stop in Denver.</font>

252
00:16:35,643 --> 00:16:38,019
<font color="#FFFFFF">What are you doing?
What's there
to even think about?</font>

253
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:39,810
<font color="#FFFFFF">You're right.</font>

254
00:16:39,852 --> 00:16:42,935
<font color="#FFFFFF">Mr. Farnsworth,
I'll take that job
in Portland.</font>

255
00:16:42,977 --> 00:16:44,351
<font color="#FFFFFF">Wait. What?</font>

256
00:16:45,810 --> 00:16:48,435
<font color="#FFFFFF">Well, there goes
my two-year chip.</font>

257
00:16:50,435 --> 00:16:52,435
<font color="#FFFFFF">Stale as the dickens.</font>

258
00:16:52,476 --> 00:16:54,852
<font color="#FFFFFF"><i>Thank you to Timothy Creehan
of Salina, Kansas,</i></font>

259
00:16:54,893 --> 00:16:57,185
<font color="#FFFFFF"><i>for sending us
this week's winning joke.</i></font>

260
00:17:04,185 --> 00:17:08,643
<font color="#FFFFFF">Francine, you're not actually
taking the job in Portland?
Think about your family.</font>

261
00:17:08,685 --> 00:17:11,685
<font color="#FFFFFF">Francine Smith
spent her whole life
thinking about her family.</font>

262
00:17:11,727 --> 00:17:14,351
<font color="#FFFFFF">And what did it do
for her? Nada.</font>

263
00:17:15,476 --> 00:17:17,144
<font color="#FFFFFF">Francine, listen to me.</font>

264
00:17:17,185 --> 00:17:20,102
<font color="#FFFFFF">Wait. You throwing that away?
This would make a perfect cape.</font>

265
00:17:21,185 --> 00:17:24,269
<font color="#FFFFFF">I am the Tender Vigilante.</font>

266
00:17:25,893 --> 00:17:29,852
<font color="#FFFFFF">This city's in pain,
and it needs my tender justice.</font>

267
00:17:31,727 --> 00:17:34,935
<font color="#FFFFFF">Oh, my God,
it's working!</font>

268
00:17:38,977 --> 00:17:40,601
<font color="#FFFFFF">Hey, sleepyhead.</font>

269
00:17:40,643 --> 00:17:43,727
<font color="#FFFFFF">Wha… What happened?
You passed out.</font>

270
00:17:43,768 --> 00:17:45,601
<font color="#FFFFFF">It's a shame.</font>

271
00:17:45,643 --> 00:17:50,351
<font color="#FFFFFF">You missed the creation
of my latest masterpiece.</font>

272
00:17:50,393 --> 00:17:53,269
<font color="#FFFFFF">She was here,
and I missed her?</font>

273
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:57,185
<font color="#FFFFFF">No, my dear Smurf,
you <i>are</i> her.</font>

274
00:17:57,227 --> 00:17:59,435
<font color="#FFFFFF">While you slumbered,
I stripped you naked,</font>

275
00:17:59,476 --> 00:18:01,810
<font color="#FFFFFF">placed a black wig on you,
put a cougar in your lap,</font>

276
00:18:01,852 --> 00:18:04,852
<font color="#FFFFFF">and…
voila!</font>

277
00:18:07,935 --> 00:18:12,601
<font color="#FFFFFF">No!</font>

278
00:18:12,643 --> 00:18:16,351
<font color="#FFFFFF">The girl in the painting
was you, wasn't it, Steve?</font>

279
00:18:16,393 --> 00:18:18,518
<font color="#FFFFFF">How… How did you know?</font>

280
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:20,810
<font color="#FFFFFF">Because I was once in love too.</font>

281
00:18:28,102 --> 00:18:33,310
<font color="#FFFFFF">The Tender Vigilante
doesn't have… insurance.</font>

282
00:18:37,393 --> 00:18:39,351
<font color="#FFFFFF">Welcome aboard, Sarah.</font>

283
00:18:56,060 --> 00:18:58,893
<font color="#FFFFFF">Ms. Blanch,
your limo is waiting
to take you to the airport.</font>

284
00:18:58,977 --> 00:19:00,269
<font color="#FFFFFF">Thank you, Jonathan.</font>

285
00:19:00,310 --> 00:19:01,893
<font color="#FFFFFF">And did you give
any thought…</font>

286
00:19:01,935 --> 00:19:03,977
<font color="#FFFFFF">to joining my family
for Christmas dinner?</font>

287
00:19:04,019 --> 00:19:06,476
<font color="#FFFFFF">We hate the thought of you
spending another holiday alone.</font>

288
00:19:06,518 --> 00:19:08,852
<font color="#FFFFFF">Thank you, Jonathan,
but I'll be working.</font>

289
00:19:08,893 --> 00:19:11,227
<font color="#FFFFFF">Plus, you know
I don't dine with robots.</font>

290
00:19:11,269 --> 00:19:13,601
<font color="#FFFFFF">Oh. But you weren't
complaining last night…</font>

291
00:19:13,643 --> 00:19:17,102
<font color="#FFFFFF">when I spent
the better part of two hours
eating your… baaa!</font>

292
00:19:32,060 --> 00:19:36,435
<font color="#FFFFFF">Broxton,
before we go to the hotel,
can we make a stop first?</font>

293
00:19:49,476 --> 00:19:52,144
<font color="#FFFFFF">I've seen enough, Broxton.</font>

294
00:19:57,893 --> 00:19:59,685
<font color="#FFFFFF">Ms. Blanch.</font>

295
00:19:59,727 --> 00:20:02,185
<font color="#FFFFFF">Back for another
concrete convention.</font>

296
00:20:02,227 --> 00:20:06,102
<font color="#FFFFFF">It's been 10 years
and three more
Garry Marshall movies.</font>

297
00:20:06,144 --> 00:20:09,227
<font color="#FFFFFF">Let me ask. Are you happy
with the life you've chosen?</font>

298
00:20:09,269 --> 00:20:12,019
<font color="#FFFFFF">No. No, I'm not.</font>

299
00:20:12,060 --> 00:20:14,601
<font color="#FFFFFF">Well, there's
always a way back.</font>

300
00:20:17,768 --> 00:20:19,435
<font color="#FFFFFF">Uh…
Sorry.</font>

301
00:20:19,476 --> 00:20:21,060
<font color="#FFFFFF">Here.</font>

302
00:20:27,810 --> 00:20:33,060
<font color="#FFFFFF">The Tender Vigilante
doesn't have… insurance.</font>

303
00:20:36,893 --> 00:20:39,685
<font color="#FFFFFF">We need to talk.
I'm you from the future.</font>

304
00:20:39,727 --> 00:20:41,518
<font color="#FFFFFF">Really?</font>

305
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:43,852
<font color="#FFFFFF">When did I get
Paulie Walnuts hair?</font>

306
00:20:43,893 --> 00:20:46,810
<font color="#FFFFFF">Don't get in that car.</font>

307
00:20:49,476 --> 00:20:52,768
<font color="#FFFFFF">Bye, guys.
Have a good day.
Wait. What about breakfast?</font>

308
00:20:52,810 --> 00:20:56,768
<font color="#FFFFFF">I'm happy
to make you breakfast
every day except Thursday.</font>

309
00:20:56,810 --> 00:20:58,435
<font color="#FFFFFF">Thursdays are for me.</font>

310
00:21:00,893 --> 00:21:03,060
<font color="#FFFFFF"><i>And from that moment on,</i></font>

311
00:21:03,102 --> 00:21:06,102
<font color="#FFFFFF"><i>Francine made Thursday</i>
her <i>day…</i></font>

312
00:21:06,144 --> 00:21:08,727
<font color="#FFFFFF"><i>a day to do
whatever she pleased.</i></font>

313
00:21:08,768 --> 00:21:11,601
<font color="#FFFFFF"><i>Yeah, girl. Do your thing.</i></font>

314
00:21:11,643 --> 00:21:13,185
<font color="#FFFFFF"><i>Get your Thursday on.</i></font>

315
00:21:19,393 --> 00:21:21,102
<font color="#FFFFFF">Man, was that close.</font>

316
00:21:54,185 --> 00:21:56,019
<font color="#FFFFFF">Bye! Have a beautiful time.</font>

317
00:21:56,185 --> 00:21:57,185
<font color="#FFFFFF">Captioned by Point.360</font>